  document.querySelector("#montePanel > .note").innerHTML = `<b>Independent random-parameter model:</b> N₀, m, R₀, S, δ, c, K, Y, and the resource-transformation tensor Dᵢβα are regenerated for every replicate. Resource-specific R₀ and S values serve as relative allocation weights and are normalized to the totals specified by the corresponding mean/fixed-value fields, keeping total initial and supplied resources constant as resource diversity increases. The CSV records all parameters and trajectories used in every replicate.`;
  methodBlocks[4].innerHTML=`<h3>5. Random Simulation and Resource-Total Normalization</h3><p>All parameters are generated independently for each replicate. Sampled R₀ and S values first define the relative allocation among resources and are then scaled so that ΣαRα,0 and ΣαSα equal the normalized totals specified in the parameter table. Increasing resource number therefore changes resource diversity without increasing the total initial or supplied resource. This normalization is not applied to manually entered resource concentrations.</p>`;
