  document.querySelector("#montePanel > .note").innerHTML=`<b>Structure-First Independent Random Model: </b>Each replicate first determines structure using specified probabilities or a fixed network:  Aᵢα  and  Pᵢβα, then samples only existing uptake and production pathways:  c, K, Y  and  D.FixedParameterscan be Objectspecified item by itemInput; Disabled pathway Parametersby  0 for calculation and recording.`;
  distMeta.find(q=>q[1]==="r0")[7]="Random draws define resource-allocation weights and are normalized to the specified total; for fixed values, enter the actual concentration of each resource";
  distMeta.find(q=>q[1]==="supply")[7]="Random draws define external-supply allocation weights and are normalized to the specified total; for fixed values, enter the actual supply concentration of each resource";
  methodBlocks[4].innerHTML=`<h3>5. Structure-First Random Simulation</h3><p>Each replicate first generates the substance-utilization structure Aᵢα; cᵢα, Kᵢα, and Yᵢα are generated only where Aᵢα=1. It then generates the metabolite-production structure Pᵢβα; Dᵢβα is generated only where the consumer utilizes the input substance and Pᵢβα=1. The structure can be resampled probabilistically for each replicate or fixed to the current network. CSV exports include both structural variables and the parameter values actually used.</p>`;

